Changes to `yi/` (the Yoshi's Island disassembly)
-------------------------------------------------

Modified continuously since 2026-05-23.

- **Symbols renamed.** Templated auto-generated labels (`CODE_xxxxxx`,
  `DATA_xxxxxx`, `YI_NorSpr*`) have been supplemented and in places replaced
  with descriptive English names derived from verified runtime behaviour —
  across the engine-core banks (Bank00, Bank01, Bank0F, Bank12, Bank13,
  Bank17), the entire SuperFX program, and the boss + sprite-engine banks
  (Bank02, Bank03, Bank05), including hundreds of dispatch-table entries. Where
  a rename would break an existing reference, the descriptive name is added as
  an alias at the same address rather than substituted. Notable corrections of
  upstream naming: the LC_LZ2 decompressor and its data pointers were renamed
  from `lz1_decompress` / `.lz1` to `lz2_decompress` / `.lz2` (the upstream name
  reflected a historical misidentification of the format); slope-direction
  constants were corrected from a down/up swap.
- **Source comments added.** Every file carries a header describing its
  contents, address ranges, and cross-references; significant routines carry
  block comments; non-obvious instructions carry end-of-line annotations. All
  442 normal sprites, 121 ambient sprites, and the level set are named and
  annotated with handler-location pointers. Sprite-slot tables are documented
  per-byte. None of this commentary is upstream's.
- **Files split and reorganised.** The 227,396-line `Routine_Macros_YI.asm` was
  split into 36 per-bank files under `yi/Banks/` plus shared routines under
  `yi/Routines/`; the 75,026-line SuperFX program was split per-bank under
  `yi/SuperFX/Banks/`; defines and memory maps were split per topic under
  `yi/Constants/` and `yi/Memory/`. The original umbrella files remain as thin
  `incsrc` wrappers.
- **Content corrections.** Entries were cross-validated against other Yoshi's
  Island disassemblies and community memory maps, which surfaced material
  corrections to upstream labels and address annotations.
- **Trimmed.** Only what the Yoshi's Island target needs is retained; support
  for the other ROMs upstream covers was removed.

Changes to `global/`
--------------------

- Trimmed to the subset the Yoshi's Island target uses; comments and
  cross-references added to match the `yi/` treatment.

Additions
---------

- `scripts/` — a Node build/extraction pipeline and an engine ported from the
  disassembly above (level decode, graphics decompression, rendering, audio).
  These ports are derived from the asm in `yi/` and are GPL-3.0 like the rest.
- `docs/` — cross-file engine reference documentation.
- `patches/` — a built-in custom-patch repository.
- `asar` / `asar.exe` / `asar-macos` — the asar assembler, a separate program
  invoked by the build, under its own license (see `asar-licenses/`).
- `M1TE.exe` — a fork of M1TE2, a separate program, under its own license (see
  `m1te-licenses/`).

Complete corresponding source, including these modifications and the build
scripts, is at https://github.com/YoriKv/shiny-egg.
